# Globs here are deliberately wide. An uncovered artifact is one `git add .` away
# from becoming tracked content that has to be scrubbed back out again.

# Bazel's convenience symlinks, any output base or cache placed inside the tree,
# and per-developer flag files. MODULE.bazel.lock and both cargo-bazel-lock.json
# files are tracked; these are not.
bazel-*
.bazel-*
/.bazelrc.user

# Cargo build trees (cargo is not the build here, but an IDE or a stray
# `cargo build` still produces one) and rustfmt's backup files.
target/
**/*.rs.bk

# The IDE's view of the build, written by `make ide`. It names absolute paths
# into a Bazel output base, so it is per-machine by construction.
rust-project.json
.rules_rust_analyzer/

# Run and diagnostic output.
*.log
*.jsonl
logs/

# Simulator reports copied beside the site for local viewing; the published
# ones are built by Bazel.
/site/reports/

# Per-machine tool configuration that names local paths.
*.local.toml
.local/

# Personal Claude Code settings (settings.json is shared).
.claude/settings.local.json

# Local secret-scanner rule overrides. Never content in this repo.
.gitleaks.local.toml

# Private per-repo agent context (CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md are shared).
CLAUDE.local.md

# Editor and OS noise.
*.swp
*~
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# allthechanges reads every entry in the fragment directories whose name does
# not start with a dot, so git sees every such entry too: a fragment the globs
# above would hide (a `bazel-…` slug) is committed, and a stray file blocks
# `make release`'s clean-tree check instead of being gathered unseen.
!/changelog.d/[!.]*
!/todo.d/[!.]*
